  "question": {
    "text": "The straight wire $A B$ carries a current $I$. The ends of the wire subtend angles $\\theta_1$ and $\\theta_2$ at the point $P$ as shown in figure. The magnetic field at the point $P$ is\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/eIzo0PjwrZuNUPihCK6GCTDX5gBm4fw_IxGyD4vWajA.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "YP9Eq",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4 \\pi d}\\left(\\sin \\theta_1-\\sin \\theta_2\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "lzdul",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4 \\pi d}\\left(\\sin \\theta_1+\\sin \\theta_2\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kefHH",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4 \\pi d}\\left(\\cos \\theta_1-\\cos \\theta_2\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NBvqU",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4 \\pi d}\\left(\\cos \\theta_1+\\cos \\theta_2\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The magnetic field at a point $P$ due to a current carrying straight wire, such that the ends of the wires, makes angle $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ (see figure) is given by\n$B=\\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4 \\pi d}(\\sin \\alpha-\\sin \\beta)$\nwhere, $d$ is the distance between the point $P$ and wire.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/2CI_LkSVH326lX_ZCnfCzZtly31MBjgQ2LMqfxWopw0.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nIn the given problem, $\\alpha=\\theta_1$ and $\\beta=\\theta_2$\n$\\therefore \\quad B=\\frac{\\mu_0 I}{4 \\pi d}\\left(\\sin \\theta_1-\\sin \\theta_2\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
